  m_text: Wooden boats, ranging from ancient dugout canoes to modern yachts, are
    vessels primarily constructed from wood, cherished for their beauty, traditional
    craftsmanship, and sustainability. While often requiring higher maintenance (such
    as addressing rot and plank movement), they offer a unique, durable, and repairable
    alternative to modern plastic boats
